1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,801
It's really in the name the term nihilism comes from the latin word nile which translates to nothing and ism which translates to ideology.
其实名字就说明了：nihilism 来自拉丁词“nile”（字幕如此），译为虚无，和“ism”，译为思想体系。

2
00:00:08,801 --> 00:00:14,720
It's the ideology of nothing but that doesn't really help us in understanding it completely.
它是“虚无的思想”，但这并不能真正帮助我们完全理解它。

3
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:20,311
Usually people confuse nihilism for pessimism but they are very different from each other.
通常人们把虚无主义和悲观主义混淆，但两者非常不同。

4
00:00:20,321 --> 00:00:22,391
Pessimists believe in the worst outcome.
悲观主义者相信最坏的结果会出现。

5
00:00:22,401 --> 00:00:26,481
They have a downtrending view of the world and tend to focus on the negatives in life.
他们对世界持一种下行的看法，往往关注生活中消极的部分，

6
00:00:26,481 --> 00:00:33,270
Because they believe that in the end evil will always overcome good and this is what makes them different.
因为他们相信，最终邪恶总会战胜善良；这就是他们的不同之处。

7
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:40,321
Pessimists believe that there's good in the world but they just don't think humans are capable of doing it at least in its entirety.
悲观主义者相信世上有善，只是不认为人类能做到，至少无法完整地做到。

8
00:00:40,321 --> 00:00:44,321
Nihilists on the other hand do not believe in anything.
而虚无主义者则什么都不相信。

9
00:00:44,321 --> 00:00:48,881
They don't believe that there's evil in the world neither do they believe that there's good in the world.
他们既不相信世界上有恶，也不相信有善。

10
00:00:48,881 --> 00:00:56,560
In the mind of the nihilist the world simply exists and humans created morality thereby creating good and evil.
在虚无主义者看来，世界只是存在，人类创造了道德，因此创造了善与恶。

11
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:59,430
Let's take the glass cup metaphor for instance.
拿玻璃杯这个比喻来说。

12
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:05,270
Optimists say you should see the glass as half full while pessimists say we should see the glass as half empty.
乐观主义者说，你应该把杯子看成半满；悲观主义者说，应该看成半空。

13
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:11,440
Nihilus they say throw the entire cup away because what does it matter if it's full or empty.
至于“nihilus”（原字幕），他们说：把整个杯子扔掉吧，是满是空又有什么关系？

14
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:17,360
Full empty good bad it's all irrelevant we're all going to die anyway.
满、空、好、坏，都不相干；反正我们终究都会死。

15
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:22,401
Nihilism is also often compared to several other philosophies like cynicism and apathy.
虚无主义也常被拿来和犬儒主义、冷漠等其他哲学或态度比较。

16
00:01:22,401 --> 00:01:29,681
But again they are all very different from one another and correctly categorizing your thoughts in these baskets may be harder than you think.
但它们也非常不同；把自己的想法正确归入这些篮子，可能比你以为的更难。

17
00:01:29,681 --> 00:01:32,801
Cynics believe that people are always motivated by self interest.
犬儒者相信，人总是被自身利益驱动。

18
00:01:32,801 --> 00:01:35,921
They don't believe that anyone can have intrinsically good motives.
他们不相信任何人会有本质上善良的动机。

19
00:01:35,921 --> 00:01:42,320
They have no faith in the human species and believe that we're all entirely selfish only fighting for our own benefit.
他们不信任人类，相信我们全都自私，只为自身利益而斗争。

20
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:50,320
However the idea that humans are not good means that in the mind of the cynic good exists out there somewhere just not in humans.
但“人类不善”这个想法，意味着在犬儒者心里，善存在于某处，只是不在人类之中。

21
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:57,030
In the mind of the nihilist nothing exists out there there's no good or evil.
在虚无主义者心里，外面什么也没有，没有善，也没有恶。

22
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:03,040
They don't see people as evil neither do they see them as good because they don't believe either of those things exist.
他们不把人看成恶，也不把人看成善，因为他们不相信这两者存在。

23
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:06,551
They're simply traits we've applied to things.
它们只是我们赋予事物的特征。

24
00:02:06,561 --> 00:02:12,870
Apathetic people just don't care they believe that there's meaning to life but they simply don't care about it.
冷漠的人只是不在乎；他们相信人生有意义，但就是不在乎这个意义。

25
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:20,601
Nihilism on the other hand is the idea that there's no grand design or purpose nothing to believe in and therefore no meaning.
另一方面，虚无主义认为，没有宏大的设计或目的，没有可相信的东西，因此也没有意义。

26
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:28,641
This brings to mind the paradox of nihilism if you believe in nothing then that nothing becomes something that you believe in.
这让人想到虚无主义的悖论：如果你什么都不信，那么这个“什么都没有”就成了你所相信的东西。

27
00:02:28,641 --> 00:02:36,471
But since you now believe in something then there is no nihilism because nihilism is the belief that there is nothing.
但既然你现在相信某个东西，就没有虚无主义了，因为虚无主义相信什么都没有。

28
00:02:36,481 --> 00:02:43,281
Nihilism is quite different from other philosophical ideas because it was first a literary invention before it ever became philosophical.
虚无主义与其他哲学观念很不一样，因为它先是一种文学发明，之后才成为哲学性的东西。

29
00:02:43,281 --> 00:02:48,081
As a result it's not clearly defined as many of the other philosophies that exist.
所以，它不像其他许多现存哲学那样定义清楚。

30
00:02:48,081 --> 00:02:51,281
Many different people explained it in many different ways.
许多人用许多不同方式解释它，

31
00:02:51,281 --> 00:03:00,001
But eventually these different definitions got categorized forming many different kinds of nihilism there's political nihilism.
最终这些不同定义被归类，形成了许多种虚无主义。其中有政治虚无主义。

32
00:03:00,001 --> 00:03:07,760
Political nihilists believe that for humanity to move forward as a species all political social and religious order must be destroyed.
政治虚无主义者认为，要让人类作为一个物种向前发展，一切政治、社会和宗教秩序都必须被摧毁。

33
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:13,440
Then there's ethical nihilism it rejects the idea of absolute ethical or moral values.
然后是伦理虚无主义，它否定绝对的伦理或道德价值。

34
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:19,921
With this type of nihilism good or bad is only defined by society and as such it shouldn't be followed.
在这种虚无主义里，善恶只由社会定义，因此不应遵循，

35
00:03:19,921 --> 00:03:26,241
If we as a species will ever attain absolute individual freedom we can kind of just do whatever we want.
如果我们这个物种要获得绝对的个人自由，就可以想做什么便做什么。

36
00:03:26,241 --> 00:03:32,081
And then we have existential nihilism it's the understanding that life has no value or meaning.
接着是存在虚无主义，即认为人生没有价值或意义。

37
00:03:32,081 --> 00:03:37,201
It's the most popular kind of nihilism and the one we've been talking about for most of this video.
这是最流行的一种，也是本视频大部分时间一直在谈的那一种。

38
00:03:37,201 --> 00:03:45,040
For nihilists the existence of things like the state religious bodies and even communal morality is a breach on our freedom as individuals.
对于虚无主义者，国家、宗教组织，甚至共同道德等事物的存在，都侵犯了我们作为个体的自由。

39
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:49,681
If we can't do absolutely anything we want to do then are we truly free.
如果不能完全想做什么就做什么，我们真的自由吗？

40
00:03:49,681 --> 00:03:58,631
Or have we simply bound ourselves by some kind of invisible mental chain for reasons we can't explain.
还是说，我们只是因为无法解释的理由，用某种看不见的精神锁链束缚了自己？
